{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-2c: boxed arithmetic round trips. (1) `int / int` and any int/float mix over inferred parameters already lowered natively but their AST type stayed `any`, so the next operator boxed both sides for fn_add and everything after it (float(), the division, the return) stayed boxed; the arithmetic operand oracle now reports the double lane the emitter produces, float() of that tree is the identity, and the proc return-lane proof admits a raw float() / native math builtin. (2) An unannotated `var` that is reassigned kept its float lane at every return but the proof refused every reassigned binding; it now proves the initializer and every write. (3) A comparison over such an inferred float local keeps an `any` AST type; the and/or gate now consumes its native 0/1 lane instead of boxing it for is_truthy.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_eval_a_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_add_p, fn_add",
        "call\tfn_float_p, fn_float",
        "call\tfn_div_p, fn_div",
        "call\tpush_d_p, push_d",
        "call\tint2it_lane_p, int2it_lane"
      ],
      "expect": [
        "ddiv\t{{r}}, {{r}}, {{r}}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_first_root_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tpush_d_p, push_d",
        "call\tfn_math_sqrt_p, fn_math_sqrt"
      ],
      "expect": [
        "call\tsqrt_p, sqrt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_count_hits_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tis_truthy_p, is_truthy",
        "call\tfn_gt_p, fn_gt",
        "call\tfn_lt_p, fn_lt",
        "call\tit2d_p, it2d",
        "call\tpush_d_p, push_d"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
